{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794729601,"nonce":"rDc15vAhtGMqmkQ0Qhj5oMZ6QaE=","message":"Native writer validated on real programs (2026-11-15, 9370bcf2). tast_dump --against, native vs Haxe exporter, zero differing: Haxe unit suite (8902 functions), Heaps 3D example (7795), Heaps 2D example (7743), the small test program (1099). scripts/native_vs_haxe.sh runs this on any build (HAXE = the haxe with the plugin, TAST_DUMP, ALLOW). tests/native_export.rs covers a whole export and positions when ASH_HAXE_NATIVE is set.\n\nHeaps found a second difference worth recording: `typedef MultiFormatCache = Map\u003cInt, {found:MultiFormat, nexts:MultiFormatCache}\u003e` names itself through an expansion that has type arguments. Both exporters cut such a type at a depth limit (Dynamic), at different depths. Now both reserve the type record before reading its arguments, so the type is a cycle in the table (9370bcf2), as structure typedefs already were. 13 typedefs in haxe.macro.*, haxe.rtti.* and a few unit tests still hit the cut (a typedef instantiated at ever larger types); both exporters cut them identically.\n\nLesson: a type cache keyed by the compiler's printed text is unsound (a class's statics structure and the class type both print Class\u003cT\u003e); any lowering that interns types should key by structure.\n\nStill open: NUC build of the toolchain (no sudo: m4, pcre2, mbedtls2 built into ~/local; OCaml 5.1.1 then Haxe in progress) for the Linux timing; layers in the native writer; overloads.","files":null}]}